{"id":"mahabharata-4-032","work":"mahabharata","part":4,"partName":"विराटपर्व","partNameEn":"Virata Parva","unit":32,"title":"द्वात्रिंशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 32 · Virata captured and rescued","summary":{"en":"In the darkness Susharman captures Virata and carries him off on his chariot. At Yudhishthira's command Bhima, restrained from uprooting a tree lest he be recognized, fights with ordinary weapons, frees Virata and captures Susharman; Yudhishthira has him released, and Virata, grateful, offers the Pandavas his kingdom.","kn":"ಕತ್ತಲಿನಲ್ಲಿ ಸುಶರ್ಮನು ವಿರಾಟನನ್ನು ಸೆರೆಹಿಡಿದು ರಥದಲ್ಲಿ ಒಯ್ಯುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನ ಆಜ್ಞೆಯಂತೆ, ಗುರುತಿಸಲ್ಪಡದಿರಲು ಮರ ಕೀಳದೆ, ಭೀಮನು ಸಾಮಾನ್ಯ ಆಯುಧಗಳಿಂದ ಹೋರಾಡಿ ವಿರಾಟನನ್ನು ಬಿಡಿಸಿ ಸುಶರ್ಮನನ್ನು ಹಿಡಿಯುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನು ಅವನನ್ನು ಬಿಡಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ, ಕೃತಜ್ಞ ವಿರಾಟನು ಪಾಂಡವರಿಗೆ ರಾಜ್ಯವನ್ನೇ ನೀಡಲು ಮುಂದಾಗುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"अँधेरे में सुशर्मा विराट को बन्दी बनाकर अपने रथ पर ले जाता है। युधिष्ठिर के आदेश पर भीम, पहचाने जाने के डर से वृक्ष उखाड़ने से रोके जाकर, साधारण शस्त्रों से लड़ते हैं, विराट को छुड़ाते हैं और सुशर्मा को पकड़ लेते हैं; युधिष्ठिर उसे छुड़वा देते हैं, और कृतज्ञ विराट पाण्डवों को अपना राज्य देने को तैयार होते हैं।","te":"చీకటిలో సుశర్మ విరాటుని బంధించి రథంపై తీసుకుపోతాడు. యుధిష్ఠిరుని ఆజ్ఞతో, గుర్తించబడకుండా చెట్టు పెకలించకుండా, భీముడు సాధారణ ఆయుధాలతో పోరాడి విరాటుని విడిపించి సుశర్మను పట్టుకుంటాడు; యుధిష్ఠిరుడు అతనిని విడిపిస్తాడు, కృతజ్ఞుడైన విరాటుడు పాండవులకు రాజ్యాన్నే ఇవ్వడానికి సిద్ధపడతాడు.","ta":"இருளில் ஸுஶர்மா விராடனைச் சிறைப்பிடித்துத் தன் தேரில் கொண்டு செல்கிறான். யுதிஷ்டிரரின் ஆணைப்படி, அடையாளம் காணப்படாதிருக்க மரத்தைப் பிடுங்காமல், பீமன் சாதாரண ஆயுதங்களால் போரிட்டு விராடனை விடுவித்து ஸுஶர்மாவைப் பிடிக்கிறான்; யுதிஷ்டிரர் அவனை விடுவிக்கச் செய்ய, நன்றியுணர்ந்த விராடன் பாண்டவர்களுக்குத் தன் அரசையே தர முன்வருகிறான்.","ml":"ഇരുട്ടിൽ സുശർമ്മാവ് വിരാടനെ പിടികൂടി രഥത്തിൽ കൊണ്ടുപോകുന്നു. യുധിഷ്ഠിരന്റെ ആജ്ഞപ്രകാരം, തിരിച്ചറിയപ്പെടുമെന്ന് ഭയന്ന് മരം പിഴുതെടുക്കാതെ ഭീമൻ സാധാരണ ആയുധങ്ങളാൽ പൊരുതുന്നു; അവൻ വിരാടനെ മോചിപ്പിച്ച് സുശർമ്മാവിനെ പിടികൂടുന്നു. യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ അദ്ദേഹത്തെ വിട്ടയക്കുന്നു; നന്ദിയുള്ള വിരാടൻ പാണ്ഡവർക്ക് തന്റെ രാജ്യം വാഗ്ദാനം ചെയ്യുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 4.32; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Thu Dec  1 2011","sections":[{"title":"गोग्रहणपर्व","titleEn":"Gograhana Parva (The cattle raid)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"तमसाभिप्लुते लोके रजसा चैव भारत ।\nव्यतिष्ठन्वै मुहूर्तं तु व्यूढानीकाः प्रहारिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the world was drowned in darkness and dust, Bharata, the fighters in their battle lines stood still for a moment."}},{"n":2,"text":"ततोऽन्धकारं प्रणुदन्नुदतिष्ठत चन्द्रमाः ।\nकुर्वाणो विमलां रात्रिं नन्दयन्क्षत्रियान्युधि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the moon rose, driving the darkness away, making the night clear and gladdening the Kshatriyas in the battle."}},{"n":3,"text":"ततः प्रकाशमासाद्य पुनर्युद्धमवर्तत ।\nघोररूपं ततस्ते स्म नावेक्षन्त परस्परम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With light restored the fighting began again, grim to see, though the soldiers could hardly see one another."}},{"n":4,"text":"ततः सुशर्मा त्रैगर्तः सह भ्रात्रा यवीयसा ।\nअभ्यद्रवन्मत्स्यराजं रथव्रातेन सर्वशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Susharman of the Trigartas, with his younger brother, attacked the king of Matsya from all sides with a host of chariots."}},{"n":5,"text":"ततो रथाभ्यां प्रस्कन्द्य भ्रातरौ क्षत्रियर्षभौ ।\nगदापाणी सुसंरब्धौ समभ्यद्रवतां हयान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the two brothers, bulls among Kshatriyas, leapt down from their chariots, mace in hand and furious, and rushed at the horses."}},{"n":6,"text":"तथैव तेषां तु बलानि तानि\nक्रुद्धान्यथान्योन्यमभिद्रवन्ति ।\nगदासिखड्गैश्च परश्वधैश्च\nप्रासैश्च तीक्ष्णाग्रसुपीतधारैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In just the same way their armies, enraged, rushed at one another with clubs, swords, axes, and spears with sharp, well-whetted points."}},{"n":7,"text":"बलं तु मत्स्यस्य बलेन राजा\nसर्वं त्रिगर्ताधिपतिः सुशर्मा ।\nप्रमथ्य जित्वा च प्रसह्य मत्स्यं\nविराटमोजस्विनमभ्यधावत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Susharman, king of the Trigartas, with his whole force pounded the Matsya army, defeated it, overpowered the Matsyas and charged at the mighty Virata."}},{"n":8,"text":"तौ निहत्य पृथग्धुर्यावुभौ च पार्ष्णिसारथी ।\nविरथं मत्स्यराजानं जीवग्राहमगृह्णताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Killing both his yoke-horses and both his rear-guard charioteers, they took the king of Matsya, now without a chariot, alive."}},{"n":9,"text":"तमुन्मथ्य सुशर्मा तु रुदतीं वधुकामिव ।\nस्यन्दनं स्वं समारोप्य प्रययौ शीघ्रवाहनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Susharman dragged him off like a weeping bride, lifted him onto his own chariot, and sped away on his swift horses."}},{"n":10,"text":"तस्मिन्गृहीते विरथे विराटे बलवत्तरे ।\nप्राद्रवन्त भयान्मत्स्यास्त्रिगर्तैरर्दिता भृशम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the powerful Virata was captured and chariotless, the Matsyas fled in terror, sorely harried by the Trigartas."}},{"n":11,"text":"तेषु संत्रास्यमानेषु कुन्तीपुत्रो युधिष्ठिरः ।\nअभ्यभाषन्महाबाहुं भीमसेनमरिंदमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As they scattered in fear, Yudhishthira, son of Kunti, spoke to the mighty-armed Bhimasena, scourge of foes."}},{"n":12,"text":"मत्स्यराजः परामृष्टस्त्रिगर्तेन सुशर्मणा ।\nतं मोक्षय महाबाहो न गच्छेद्द्विषतां वशम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The king of Matsya has been seized by Susharman of the Trigartas. Free him, mighty-armed Bhima, so that he does not fall into the enemies' power."}},{"n":13,"text":"उषिताः स्मः सुखं सर्वे सर्वकामैः सुपूजिताः ।\nभीमसेन त्वया कार्या तस्य वासस्य निष्कृतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"We have all lived here happily, honored with every comfort. Bhimasena, you must repay him for that stay.\""}},{"text":"भीमसेन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhimasena said:"}},{"n":14,"text":"अहमेनं परित्रास्ये शासनात्तव पार्थिव ।\nपश्य मे सुमहत्कर्म युध्यतः सह शत्रुभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I will rescue him on your command, king. Watch my great deeds as I fight the enemy."}},{"n":15,"text":"स्वबाहुबलमाश्रित्य तिष्ठ त्वं भ्रातृभिः सह ।\nएकान्तमाश्रितो राजन्पश्य मेऽद्य पराक्रमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Rely on the strength of your own arms and stay with your brothers; stand aside, king, and watch my valor today."}},{"n":16,"text":"सुस्कन्धोऽयं महावृक्षो गदारूप इव स्थितः ।\nएनमेव समारुज्य द्रावयिष्यामि शात्रवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"This great tree with its fine trunk stands like a mace. I will tear it up and with it drive off the enemy.\""}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":17,"text":"तं मत्तमिव मातङ्गं वीक्षमाणं वनस्पतिम् ।\nअब्रवीद्भ्रातरं वीरं धर्मराजो युधिष्ठिरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As Bhima, like a rutting elephant, eyed the tree, Yudhishthira, king of dharma, spoke to his brave brother."}},{"n":18,"text":"मा भीम साहसं कार्षीस्तिष्ठत्वेष वनस्पतिः ।\nमा त्वा वृक्षेण कर्माणि कुर्वाणमतिमानुषम् ।\nजनाः समवबुध्येरन्भीमोऽयमिति भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Do not be rash, Bhima; let that tree be. If people see you doing superhuman deeds with a tree, Bharata, they will realize this is Bhima."}},{"n":19,"text":"अन्यदेवायुधं किंचित्प्रतिपद्यस्व मानुषम् ।\nचापं वा यदि वा शक्तिं निस्त्रिंशं वा परश्वधम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Take some other, human weapon instead, a bow, a spear, a sword or an axe."}},{"n":20,"text":"यदेव मानुषं भीम भवेदन्यैरलक्षितम् ।\nतदेवायुधमादाय मोक्षयाशु महीपतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whatever human weapon others will not notice, Bhima, take that and quickly free the king."}},{"n":21,"text":"यमौ च चक्ररक्षौ ते भवितारौ महाबलौ ।\nव्यूहतः समरे तात मत्स्यराजं परीप्सतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The two mighty twins will guard your wheels, dear brother, as you form up for battle, wishing to rescue the king of Matsya.\""}},{"n":22,"text":"ततः समस्तास्ते सर्वे तुरगानभ्यचोदयन् ।\nदिव्यमस्त्रं विकुर्वाणास्त्रिगर्तान्प्रत्यमर्षणाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then all of them, burning with anger, spurred their horses against the Trigartas, displaying divine weapons."}},{"n":23,"text":"तान्निवृत्तरथान्दृष्ट्वा पाण्डवान्सा महाचमूः ।\nवैराटी परमक्रुद्धा युयुधे परमाद्भुतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the Pandavas turn their chariots back, that great Matsya army, filled with fury, fought most wondrously."}},{"n":24,"text":"सहस्रं न्यवधीत्तत्र कुन्तीपुत्रो युधिष्ठिरः ।\nभीमः सप्तशतान्योधान्परलोकमदर्शयत् ।\nनकुलश्चापि सप्तैव शतानि प्राहिणोच्छरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There Yudhishthira, son of Kunti, killed a thousand; Bhima sent seven hundred warriors to the next world; Nakula too sent seven hundred with his arrows."}},{"n":25,"text":"शतानि त्रीणि शूराणां सहदेवः प्रतापवान् ।\nयुधिष्ठिरसमादिष्टो निजघ्ने पुरुषर्षभः ।\nभित्त्वा तां महतीं सेनां त्रिगर्तानां नरर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"The mighty Sahadeva, bull among men, at Yudhishthira's bidding slew three hundred heroes, breaking through that great Trigarta army."}},{"n":26,"text":"ततो युधिष्ठिरो राजा त्वरमाणो महारथः ।\nअभिद्रुत्य सुशर्माणं शरैरभ्यतुदद्भृशम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then King Yudhishthira, the great charioteer, hurried at Susharman and tormented him sorely with arrows."}},{"n":27,"text":"सुशर्मापि सुसंक्रुद्धस्त्वरमाणो युधिष्ठिरम् ।\nअविध्यन्नवभिर्बाणैश्चतुर्भिश्चतुरो हयान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Susharman, also enraged and hurrying, pierced Yudhishthira with nine arrows and his four horses with four."}},{"n":28,"text":"ततो राजन्नाशुकारी कुन्तीपुत्रो वृकोदरः ।\nसमासाद्य सुशर्माणमश्वानस्य व्यपोथयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Bhima, the quick-acting son of Kunti, reached Susharman, O king, and struck down his horses."}},{"n":29,"text":"पृष्ठगोपौ च तस्याथ हत्वा परमसायकैः ।\nअथास्य सारथिं क्रुद्धो रथोपस्थादपाहरत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Killing his two rear guards with fine arrows, he angrily pulled his charioteer off the chariot's platform."}},{"n":30,"text":"चक्ररक्षश्च शूरश्च शोणाश्वो नाम विश्रुतः ।\nस भयाद्द्वैरथं दृष्ट्वा त्रैगर्तं प्राजहत्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The brave wheel-guard named Shonashva, seeing a duel between chariots, fled in fear and abandoned the Trigarta."}},{"n":31,"text":"ततो विराटः प्रस्कन्द्य रथादथ सुशर्मणः ।\nगदामस्य परामृश्य तमेवाजघ्निवान्बली ।\nस चचार गदापाणिर्वृद्धोऽपि तरुणो यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Virata leapt down from Susharman's chariot, seized his mace, and struck him with it; though old, he moved about mace in hand like a young man."}},{"n":32,"text":"भीमस्तु भीमसंकाशो रथात्प्रस्कन्द्य कुण्डली ।\nत्रिगर्तराजमादत्त सिंहः क्षुद्रमृगं यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhima, terrible as his name, leapt from his chariot, in earrings, and seized the king of the Trigartas, as a lion seizes a little deer."}},{"n":33,"text":"तस्मिन्गृहीते विरथे त्रिगर्तानां महारथे ।\nअभज्यत बलं सर्वं त्रैगर्तं तद्भयातुरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When that great Trigarta chariot-fighter was captured and chariotless, the whole Trigarta army broke, struck with fear."}},{"n":34,"text":"निवर्त्य गास्ततः सर्वाः पाण्डुपुत्रा महाबलाः ।\nअवजित्य सुशर्माणं धनं चादाय सर्वशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the mighty sons of Pandu brought back all the cattle, defeated Susharman and took back all the wealth."}},{"n":35,"text":"स्वबाहुबलसंपन्ना ह्रीनिषेधा यतव्रताः ।\nसंग्रामशिरसो मध्ये तां रात्रिं सुखिनोऽवसन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Rich in the strength of their own arms, restrained by modesty and firm in their vows, they spent that night happily at the head of the battlefield."}},{"n":36,"text":"ततो विराटः कौन्तेयानतिमानुषविक्रमान् ।\nअर्चयामास वित्तेन मानेन च महारथान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Virata honored the sons of Kunti, great warriors of superhuman prowess, with wealth and respect."}},{"text":"विराट उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Virata said:"}},{"n":37,"text":"यथैव मम रत्नानि युष्माकं तानि वै तथा ।\nकार्यं कुरुत तैः सर्वे यथाकामं यथासुखम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Whatever jewels are mine are yours as well. Use them all as you wish and as it pleases you."}},{"n":38,"text":"ददान्यलंकृताः कन्या वसूनि विविधानि च ।\nमनसश्चाप्यभिप्रेतं यद्वः शत्रुनिबर्हणाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I will give you adorned maidens and riches of every kind, and whatever else your hearts desire, destroyers of enemies."}},{"n":39,"text":"युष्माकं विक्रमादद्य मुक्तोऽहं स्वस्तिमानिह ।\nतस्माद्भवन्तो मत्स्यानामीश्वराः सर्व एव हि ॥","meaning":{"en":"By your valor today I am freed and safe here, so all of you are lords of the Matsyas.\""}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":40,"text":"तथाभिवादिनं मत्स्यं कौरवेयाः पृथक्पृथक् ।\nऊचुः प्राञ्जलयः सर्वे युधिष्ठिरपुरोगमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the king of Matsya spoke so, the Kauravas, with Yudhishthira at their head, each with folded hands answered him in turn."}},{"n":41,"text":"प्रतिनन्दाम ते वाक्यं सर्वं चैव विशां पते ।\nएतेनैव प्रतीताः स्मो यत्त्वं मुक्तोऽद्य शत्रुभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"We welcome all your words, lord of men. We are content with this alone, that you are freed today from your enemies.\""}},{"n":42,"text":"अथाब्रवीत्प्रीतमना मत्स्यराजो युधिष्ठिरम् ।\nपुनरेव महाबाहुर्विराटो राजसत्तमः ।\nएहि त्वामभिषेक्ष्यामि मत्स्यराजोऽस्तु नो भवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the king of Matsya, the best of kings and mighty-armed Virata, spoke again to Yudhishthira with a glad heart."}},{"n":43,"text":"मनसश्चाप्यभिप्रेतं यत्ते शत्रुनिबर्हण ।\nतत्तेऽहं संप्रदास्यामि सर्वमर्हति नो भवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Come, I will anoint you; be our king of Matsya. I will give you whatever your heart desires, destroyer of enemies; you deserve it all."}},{"n":44,"text":"रत्नानि गाः सुवर्णं च मणिमुक्तमथापि वा ।\nवैयाघ्रपद्य विप्रेन्द्र सर्वथैव नमोऽस्तु ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Jewels, cows, gold, gems and pearls, O Vaiyaghrapadya, best of Brahmins: in every way, my homage to you."}},{"n":45,"text":"त्वत्कृते ह्यद्य पश्यामि राज्यमात्मानमेव च ।\nयतश्च जातः संरम्भः स च शत्रुर्वशं गतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Because of you I see my kingdom and my very self today, and the enemy who started this attack has come under our power.\""}},{"n":46,"text":"ततो युधिष्ठिरो मत्स्यं पुनरेवाभ्यभाषत ।\nप्रतिनन्दामि ते वाक्यं मनोज्ञं मत्स्य भाषसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Yudhishthira answered the king of Matsya once more: \"I welcome these pleasing words you speak, king of Matsya."}},{"n":47,"text":"आनृशंस्यपरो नित्यं सुसुखः सततं भव ।\nगच्छन्तु दूतास्त्वरितं नगरं तव पार्थिव ।\nसुहृदां प्रियमाख्यातुं घोषयन्तु च ते जयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Be ever intent on kindness and always be well content. Let messengers go swiftly to your city to tell your friends the glad news and proclaim your victory.\""}},{"n":48,"text":"ततस्तद्वचनान्मत्स्यो दूतान्राजा समादिशत् ।\nआचक्षध्वं पुरं गत्वा संग्रामे विजयं मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"At his word the king of Matsya sent out messengers: \"Go to the city and announce my victory in battle."}},{"n":49,"text":"कुमाराः समलंकृत्य पर्यागच्छन्तु मे पुरात् ।\nवादित्राणि च सर्वाणि गणिकाश्च स्वलंकृताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Let the princes come out from my city, adorned, with all the musical instruments and richly dressed courtesans.\""}},{"n":50,"text":"ते गत्वा केवलां रात्रिमथ सूर्योदयं प्रति ।\nविराटस्य पुराभ्याशे दूता जयमघोषयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Traveling through the whole night, at sunrise the messengers proclaimed the victory near Virata's city."}}]}]}